---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description = 'How World Battery Hub handles personal information: what we collect when you email us, what we never collect, retention, your rights and contacts.';
const canonical = '/privacy-policy/';

const jsonLd = [{
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Privacy Policy',
  description,
  url: 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/privacy-policy/',
}];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  dateModified="2026-09-21"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Legal · Last reviewed 2026-09-21</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        World Battery Hub is a knowledge and data platform. We designed it to collect as little personal
        information as possible — which is why this policy is short, and why there is no cookie banner on this
        site.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> There are no user accounts, no comment system, no newsletter and no
        contact form on this site. We use <strong>no advertising cookies, no third-party analytics and no
        tracking pixels</strong>. The only personal information we hold is what you choose to send us by
        email, plus standard server logs kept by our hosting provider.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated by World Battery Hub ("we", "us"), a battery knowledge and data platform.
        For any privacy question or request, contact
        <a href="mailto:editorial@worldbatteryhub.com">editorial@worldbatteryhub.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No user accounts, logins or profiles.</li>
        <li>No comment system or public posting.</li>
        <li>No newsletter subscription and no marketing email list.</li>
        <li>No contact form — enquiries reach us by email.</li>
        <li>No advertising cookies, no social-media pixels, no third-party analytics, no cross-site tracking,
            no fingerprinting and no session recording.</li>
        <li>No sale, rental or trading of personal information.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. What we do collect</h2>
      <p>
        Only two categories of information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What you send us.</strong> If you email us — for example to report a correction, ask a
            question, request data or make a licensing enquiry — we receive your email address, whatever name
            and organisation you include, and the content of your message and attachments.</li>
        <li><strong>Standard server logs.</strong> Our hosting and content-delivery provider records routine
            technical information when a page is requested — such as IP address, browser and device type,
            requested URL and timestamp — for security, abuse prevention and capacity planning.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not ask for and do not want to receive special-category or sensitive personal data. Please do
        not send it.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not set advertising or analytics cookies, and it stores nothing about you in your
        browser beyond what is needed to load the page. Our hosting and content-delivery provider may set a
        strictly necessary security cookie to protect the site against bots and abuse; it is not used to
        profile you. Because no non-essential cookies are used, no consent banner is required on this site. If
        we ever add analytics or marketing cookies, we will update this policy and ask for consent where the
        law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How we use what we receive</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to answer your email, including correction reports, editorial questions and data enquiries;</li>
        <li>to keep records of corrections and editorial correspondence;</li>
        <li>to protect the website against abuse and to keep it available;</li>
        <li>to comply with legal obligations where they apply.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use your information for advertising, and we do not add you to a mailing list.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Legal bases</h2>
      <p>
        Where the GDPR, UK GDPR or similar laws apply, we process personal information on the basis of our
        <em>legitimate interests</em> in operating and protecting this platform and in answering you; on
        <em>your request</em> or the performance of a contract where you have asked us for something (for
        example a data licence); and on <em>legal obligation</em> where records must be kept.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell or trade personal information. We share it only where necessary: with our hosting,
        content-delivery, email and IT service providers (who process it on our instructions); with
        professional advisers such as accountants; or with authorities where we are legally required to
        disclose. We do not share it with advertising networks, data brokers or analytics providers.
      </p>

      <h2>8. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Our service providers may process information in countries other than your own, including where the
        website is hosted or delivered. Where personal information is transferred internationally we take
        steps to keep it protected — including contractual measures with our providers and limiting transfers
        to what is necessary for the purposes above.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry and correction correspondence is kept for as long as needed to handle the matter and maintain
        an editorial record, then deleted or archived in a form that no longer identifies you where possible.
        Server logs are retained by our hosting provider for a short operational period. Where a law requires
        us to keep something (for example an accounting record), we keep it for as long as that law requires.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use technical and organisational measures to protect the information we hold, including restricted
        access to our systems and accounts, transport encryption on this website where available, and limiting
        collection to what we actually need. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to applicable law — including the GDPR/UK GDPR and applicable U.S. state privacy laws — you
        may request to access the personal information we hold about you, correct it, delete it, restrict or
        object to certain processing, receive it in a portable format, or withdraw consent where processing is
        based on consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:editorial@worldbatteryhub.com">editorial@worldbatteryhub.com</a> and we will
        respond within a reasonable period and within any deadline set by applicable law. If you are not
        satisfied with our response, you may complain to your local data-protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This platform is published for engineers, professionals, students and researchers. It is not directed
        at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy when our practices or legal obligations change. The version published on this
        page, with the review date above, is the current version.
      </p>

      <h2>Related policies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a></li>
        <li><a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a></li>
        <li><a href="/data-use-and-citation/">Data Use &amp; Citation</a></li>
        <li><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
